 :consequences
 {:registry-update {:status "completed"
                    :repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-862"
                    :business-id "cloud-itonami-isic-862"
                    :maturity :implemented
                    :required-technologies [:identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :langgraph-clj]
                    :operating-states [:intake :advise :govern :decide :approve :commit :audit]}
  :repo-scaffold "pushed to main"
  :tests {:count 9
          :assertions 84
          :failures 0
          :errors 0
          :namespaces [:advisor-test :governor-test :governor-contract-test :phase-test :store-contract-test]}
  :lint {:errors 0 :warnings 11}
  :demo {:scenarios 10 :completed-without-error? true}}

 :rationale
 "Outpatient clinics are clinically-central industries (like hospitals). The core
  business IS clinical care delivery. Therefore this actor's scope must be strictly
  administrative/facility coordination, with maximally-conservative clinical-content
  scanning to prevent any patient-care/clinical-decision/diagnostic/treatment language
  whatsoever, even at the periphery. Unlike hospitals (which coordinate bed/room
  assignment and visitor access), outpatient clinics coordinate appointment scheduling,
  referral logistics, supply requests, staff shifts, and facility safety concerns.
  The test legitimate-facility-safety-concern-is-not-scope-excluded verifies that
  real facility issues are NOT self-blocked by this scanning. Patient-safety concerns
  (vital sign change, clinical emergency) are explicitly out-of-scope — they must
  route through actual clinical staff/systems, not this coordination actor."

 :alternative-approaches
 [{:name "Broader outpatient clinic scope"
   :rejected-because "Clinics are clinically central. A broader scope would risk clinical decisions bleeding into coordination logic, violating the principle that this actor must be permanently clinically-read-only. Narrower is safer."}
  {:name "Unified medical practice actor covering all medical/dental settings"
   :rejected-because "Hospitals (isic-861) and outpatient clinics (isic-862) have fundamentally different operational logistics. Hospitals coordinate bed/room management; clinics coordinate appointments/referrals. They need separate actors with different operation sets."}]
}
